course: dictionary
lesson: 8678
title: One word, many meanings: see
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word see has many meanings, so the context tells you which one to use. Most often it means to notice something with your eyes: «Albino animals often see poorly» means their eyesight is weak. Ask yourself: is someone looking, understanding, meeting or finding out?
explain: «Some pictures, like the duck-rabbit, can be seen in two ways.» Here see is about what your mind takes from a picture, not only what your eyes take in. «I see what you mean» means I understand you. Test the meaning in the sentence: if it still makes sense, you have found it.
explain: See can also mean to meet or visit someone, as in see the doctor, or to take care of something, as in «I'll see to the dishes». In a book, «see page 4» tells you to look at that page. When you leave someone, you can say «see you», which means goodbye.
fact: See means to notice something with your eyes.
fact: See can mean to understand: «I see what you mean» means «I understand».
fact: See can mean to meet or visit someone, as in see the doctor.
fact: «See you» means goodbye, and it tells the other person you will meet again.
fact: In 1609-1610 Galileo's homemade telescope showed moons going round Jupiter, so people could see things no one had seen before.
exercise: «Albino animals often see poorly.» What does see mean here? | They hide from people | *Their eyesight is weak | They do not like going to the doctor | They are not good at understanding
exercise: Maya says, «I see what you mean.» What does she mean? | *She understands what you are saying | She is saying goodbye | She is going to visit you | She has spotted a mean person
exercise: «I'll see to the dishes.» What does see to mean here? | To break the dishes | *To take care of the dishes | To meet the dishes | To look at the dishes only
test: «Let's see what happens next.» In this sentence, see means: | To find out | *To find out what will happen | To feel sad | To say hello
test: What does see mean in «see page 4»? | To buy a new book | *To look at that part of the book | To read the book out loud | To close the book
exam: Which meaning of see is used in «See you on Monday at school!»? | *Goodbye, I will meet you again | To take care of a thing | To understand a rule | To notice with your eyes
